# mt#4577: Martian Code Review Bench outputs are the exception to the blanket ignore
# above — NOT regenerable without re-running a ~$11 external benchmark pass against a
# pinned third-party commit, and committing them (SC2) is this task's own acceptance
# criterion. Everything else under results/ (paired-eval-runner.ts's own timestamped
# comparative runs) stays ignored per the rationale above.
!services/reviewer/eval/results/benchmark_data.json
!services/reviewer/eval/results/benchmark_data-generation-meta.json
!services/reviewer/eval/results/REPORT.md
# Negating the directory entry is sufficient — results/* only matches direct children of
# results/, so once gpt-5.2-judge/ itself is un-ignored, nothing further excludes files
# nested inside it. A second, file-level negation here would be redundant (verified via
# `git check-ignore -v` against all three committed files in this directory).
!services/reviewer/eval/results/gpt-5.2-judge/
*.tsbuildinfo

# mt#4748 SC6: the two patterns that used to live here
# (**/.minsky/*-calibration.jsonl, **/.minsky/*-evaluations.jsonl — mt#2667)
# are RETIRED, not merely removed. The calibration/evaluation detector family
# no longer writes into any working tree at all — dispatcher.ts's
# calibrationLogPath/evaluationLogPath now resolve under the state dir,
# project-keyed (~/.local/state/minsky/projects/<key>/), so there is no
# working-tree path left for a pattern to cover. A denylist here would be
# permanently dead weight that a future reader could mistake for coverage
# still in force. See docs/architecture/guard-calibration-stream-inventory.md
# and ADR-028 §D4 (amended in the same change) for the new location.
#
# Backups Minsky's own MCP config writer takes before modifying .mcp.json
# (mt#2492). Same class as the logs above — a tool writing into the working tree
# with nothing ignoring it — but a different producer and directory, so it gets
# its own line rather than being folded into the globs. Note .mcp.json itself is
# gitignored with ZERO commits, so its git history is NOT a backup: these files
# are the only prior copies of that config that exist. Ignore them; do not
# delete them.
#
# ANY DEPTH, deliberately — no leading slash. `projectConfigPath()` in
# src/mcp/setup/local-http-config.ts joins `.mcp.json` onto whatever projectRoot
# it is handed, and a session workspace is a project root, so a backup can land
# outside the repo root. Verified 2026-08-29: `git check-ignore -v` matches this
# line against `tmpprobe/nested/.mcp.json.minsky-backup-<stamp>`. Do not "fix"
# this by adding a leading slash (PR #3474 R1 read it as root-only).
.mcp.json.minsky-backup-*
**/.minsky/subagent-model-mismatch.jsonl
**/.minsky/calibration-review-watermarks.json
# Sweep-time claims on a calibration log (mt#4164) — the same class of local
# runtime state as the watermark store above, written on every read-only sweep
# and emptied at ack. Tracking it would put one machine's in-flight passes into
# every other checkout.
**/.minsky/calibration-review-claims.json
# Transient lock dir guarding the store above (mt#3899). A crashed pass can
# leave one behind; the next pass reaps it by mtime. Never a tracked artifact.
**/.minsky/calibration-review-watermarks.lock/
**/.minsky/calibration-review-cadence-last-warned.json
# mt#2358: the main-workspace mutation observer's last-observed dirty set. Local
# state, rewritten on every Bash call — tracking it would make the observer the
# single largest source of the very dirty-tree noise it exists to report.
**/.minsky/main-workspace-mutation-baseline.json

