# verification passes (e.g. via chrome-devtools / playwright screenshotting).
# These are working artifacts, not committed deliverables.
/.cockpit-*.png

# mt#2609: repo-hygiene cleanup — these directories/files were tracked via
# accidental `git add .` sweeps (mt#2607 audit findings 1-3, 6-8) and have been
# removed from tracking. Ignored here so a future broad `git add .` cannot
# re-introduce the same class of cruft.
/backups/
/eslint-baselines/
/scripts/results/
/scripts/.import-reports/
.specstory/
# mt#2609: the literal `~/` directory tracked via an unquoted tilde-expansion
# bug in some historical command (reviewer-bot suggestion, PR #1787 R1).
/~/

# Per-session detector state written at runtime, keyed by session id (e.g.
# unasked-direction postmortem output). Machine-local: it regenerates, and a
# `session_commit --all` in any session would otherwise sweep in state files
# belonging to OTHER sessions — which is exactly how one landed in PR #2341.
/.minsky/state/

# Latency measurements written by scripts/verify-cockpit-navigation-latency.ts
# (mt#3696). Timings are a property of the machine and its load at the moment of
# the run, not of the repo: committing them would produce a large diff on every
# run and invite reading one machine's numbers as a project-wide baseline.
/scripts/cockpit-navigation-latency-results.json
/scripts/peek-drag-frames-results.json

# Per-run measurement output from scripts/verify-supavisor-slot-reclaim.ts
# (mt#4547). Each run records a point-in-time reading of a SHARED tenant gauge
# whose value depends on what the rest of the fleet happens to be doing, so a
# committed copy would go stale immediately and invite being read as a baseline.
# The durable finding lives on the task and in the PR body instead.
/scripts/supavisor-slot-reclaim-baseline.json
/scripts/supavisor-slot-reclaim-arm-a.json
/scripts/supavisor-slot-reclaim-arm-b.json
